  "native": "República dos Estados Unidos do Brasil",
  "roman": "República dos Estados Unidos do Brasil"
 },
 "capsule": "The Brazilian Republic denotes federative republican Brazil across the oligarchic 'Old Republic' (1889–1930), the Vargas-led provisional and constitutional governments of the 1930s, and the post-1945 liberal-democratic Fourth Republic (1946–1964) that followed the fall of the Estado Novo, continuing nominally as the United States of Brazil into the early military regime until the 1967 constitution renamed the country. Coffee oligarchs, urban industrializers, and populist and military factions alternated in power across this span, punctuated by the 1930 and 1937 Vargas coups and the 1945 and 1964 military interventions. This broad republican-federative designation is distinct from the centralized Estado Novo 'Unitary State of Brazil' and the later 'Federated Republic' and 'Republic of Brazil' sharing this identifier.",
 "citations": [
